---
import Layout from '../layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Compound Interest Calculator | RIPL Wealth" description="Explore how a starting balance, regular contributions, time and an assumed annual rate affect a hypothetical balance. Annual compounding, with a year-by-year chart.">
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">YOUR MONEY. TIME. A CLEARER PICTURE.</div><h1>Small decisions today.<br/><span class="ripl-gold">More possibilities tomorrow.</span></h1><p class="lead">Explore compound interest with different starting amounts, contributions and timelines. These numbers show what your assumptions produce, not what an investment will earn.</p><p class="small">Compounding is set to annually. You choose how often you contribute.</p></div></section>
<section class="section questions"><div class="wrap"><div class="compound-grid" data-compound>
<form class="compound-controls" novalidate>
<label for="compound-start">Starting amount ($)<input id="compound-start" name="principal" type="number" min="0" max="1000000000" step="any" value="10000" inputmode="decimal" required/></label>
<label for="compound-years">Years to grow<input id="compound-years" name="years" type="number" min="0" max="60" step="1" value="10" inputmode="numeric" required/></label>
<label for="compound-rate">Assumed annual rate (%)<input id="compound-rate" name="rate" type="number" min="-100" max="30" step="any" value="5" inputmode="decimal" required/></label>
<label for="compound-add">Additional contribution ($)<input id="compound-add" name="contribution" type="number" min="0" max="10000000" step="any" value="100" inputmode="decimal" required/></label>
<label for="compound-frequency">Contribution frequency<select id="compound-frequency" name="frequency"><option value="monthly">Monthly</option><option value="annually">Annually</option></select></label>
<p class="small">The 5% starting assumption is an example you can change. It is not a RIPL forecast or recommendation.</p>
<button type="submit" class="btn">Update Illustration</button><p class="compound-error" role="alert" data-calc-error></p>
</form>
<div class="compound-results" data-calc-results hidden>
<div class="compound-stats" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><div class="compound-total"><span>Hypothetical ending balance</span><strong data-calc-total></strong></div><div><span>Total money contributed</span><strong data-calc-deposits></strong></div><div><span>Hypothetical growth or loss</span><strong data-calc-growth></strong></div></div>
<div class="compound-legend"><span>Hypothetical balance</span><span>Your contributions</span></div>
<svg class="compound-chart" viewBox="0 0 720 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="compound-chart-title compound-chart-desc"><title id="compound-chart-title">Hypothetical balance and contributions over time</title><desc id="compound-chart-desc">A chart showing the annual balance and total contributions. The year-by-year table below contains the same values.</desc><g data-calc-chart></g></svg>
<p class="small" data-calc-summary></p>
<details><summary>See the year-by-year numbers</summary><div class="compound-table-wrap"><table class="compound-table"><caption>Hypothetical annual illustration</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Contributions</th><th scope="col">Growth or loss</th><th scope="col">Balance</th></tr></thead><tbody data-calc-table></tbody></table></div></details>
</div>
</div><noscript><p>Please enable JavaScript to use this calculator. You can also <a href="/contact/">talk to the team</a> about the decisions you are exploring.</p></noscript>
<div class="compound-disclaimer"><h2>Understand the assumptions.</h2><p>Interest or return is credited once a year. Starting money and prior years’ balances receive the full assumed annual rate. Monthly contributions are added at the end of each month and earn simple prorated interest for the remaining months until the annual crediting date. Annual contributions are added at year end and first earn interest in the following year. Contributions remain constant, earnings stay invested, and no withdrawals are modeled.</p><p>The illustration assumes the same annual rate every year. Actual investments can rise or fall, and the timing of gains and losses affects outcomes. Negative rates show a hypothetical loss scenario. The calculator does not model taxes, advisory fees, investment expenses, inflation, changing rates or the sequence of investment returns. Those factors can materially reduce the amount available to you and its purchasing power.</p><p>This is an educational mathematical illustration, not a forecast, financial plan, recommendation, offer, or representation of any RIPL portfolio’s past or future performance. Results are rounded for display. They do not establish whether you can retire, what you can safely spend, or whether an investment fits your situation. All investing involves risk, including loss of principal. No rate, balance, growth or financial-freedom outcome is guaranteed.</p></div>
</div></section><section class="final-cta"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PUT THE NUMBERS IN CONTEXT</div><h2>A number is a starting point.<br/><span class="ripl-gold">Your life gives it purpose.</span></h2><p>Let’s connect the possibilities with what you actually want your money to do.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the Team</a><a class="text-link" href="/financial-freedom/">Explore Financial Freedom →</a></div></div></section>
<script>import '../compound-calculator.js';</script>
</Layout>
